 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/golf-communities/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you have to join the club to live in a Myrtle Beach golf community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Almost never. Membership is optional at Barefoot, Prestwick, Pawleys Plantation, and even private Wachesaw Plantation, though non-members there get no amenities since everything belongs to the club. Where the course is public, like Arrowhead, Wild Wing, Blackmoor, Legends, International Club, and TPC Myrtle Beach, there is no membership to join at all."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many golf courses does Myrtle Beach have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"More than 80 championship courses, per Visit Myrtle Beach's current figure. The 100-course number still quoted around the internet is outdated. The oldest is Pine Lakes International, opened 1927; the most famous is the Dunes Golf and Beach Club, a 1948 Robert Trent Jones Sr. design that hosts the PGA Tour's Myrtle Beach Classic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Barefoot Resort golf transfer fee?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Resale buyers of Barefoot homes that carry a golf membership pay a $2,750 transfer fee to Barefoot Resort Golf Club, with enrollment required within 60 days of closing. Dues run $205 a month for golf and social access or $85 for social only, covering the Dye, Love, Fazio, and Norman courses."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TPC Myrtle Beach private?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It is the only TPC in South Carolina and it welcomes public play, which is rare for the brand. It anchors the Prince Creek master plan in Murrells Inlet, where villages range from the low $300,000s to the $600,000s and up, including the Seasons 55+ community."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach golf communities are gated with a guard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tidewater Plantation, Wachesaw Plantation, Willbrook Plantation and DeBordieu Colony have a guard gate or guard house. Grande Dunes and Barefoot Resort are gated only in some sections. Our guide to gated communities near Myrtle Beach has the map."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest golf community in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Legends' Turnberry Park condos at $150,000 to $215,000 and Arrowhead condos from about $175,000 are the verified low end for buying in. For houses, Blackmoor pairs a Gary Player course with roughly a $35 monthly HOA, the lowest fee we verified in any Grand Strand golf community."}}]}</script>
