 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the cost of living cheaper in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The biggest difference is the house. A typical home here sells for about $342,000, against about $737,000 in the New York area and about $742,000 in Boston. Day to day costs are closer to average, and rent is about 17 percent below the national average."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What salary do I need to live in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on where you live now, which is what the calculator on this page is for. On the price index behind the calculator, someone earning $70,000 in Los Angeles would need about $43,000 here for the same buying power. Not every move saves money. Someone coming from Montgomery, Alabama would need about the same, and from a few smaller southern metros slightly more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach cheaper than Charlotte or Raleigh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the house, yes. A typical home here is about $342,000. Charlotte is about $389,000 and Raleigh about $437,000. Property tax on a main home is also lower here because South Carolina taxes an owner-occupied home on 4 percent of its value."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What costs more in Myrtle Beach than people expect?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two things. South Carolina taxes your car every year, which most northern states do not, and that runs a few hundred dollars per vehicle. A second home or rental is taxed at about three times the rate of a main home."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where does the calculator get its data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Home values and rents come from Zillow. Everything else comes from the US Bureau of Economic Analysis, which measures what things 