 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/healthcare/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What hospitals are in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Six hospitals serve Horry and Georgetown counties. Grand Strand Medical Center in Myrtle Beach has 403 beds and Conway Medical Center has 222. McLeod Health Seacoast in Little River has 155, Tidelands Georgetown Memorial 131, Tidelands Waccamaw in Murrells Inlet 124, and McLeod Health Loris 50. Three more are being built or opening."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a trauma center in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Grand Strand Medical Center is an adult Level I trauma center and a pediatric Level II trauma center. Tidelands Waccamaw in Murrells Inlet is a designated adult Level IV trauma center."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are new hospitals being built in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two are under construction. McLeod Health held a ribbon cutting for its 48-bed Carolina Forest hospital on August 27, 2026, and said it would open to patients that fall. Grand Strand Health broke ground in February 2026 on the 59-bed South Strand Hospital on the US-17 Bypass, due late 2027. Tidelands Health has begun site work on a 36-bed hospital at SC-31 and SC-707, due late 2028."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What awards and certifications do Myrtle Beach hospitals hold?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Healthgrades placed Grand Strand Medical Center among America’s 250 Best Hospitals in 2023 and 2024, and among America’s 100 Best for stroke care and critical care from 2023 through 2025. Tidelands Waccamaw and Tidelands Georgetown are Joint Commission-certified advanced primary stroke centers. Conway Medical Center runs an accredited family medicine residency sponsored by Campbell University."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a VA hospital in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is a VA outpatient clinic at 1800 Airpark Drive in Myrtle Beach, part of VA Charleston Health Care, offering primary care, mental health, geriatrics, laboratory, imaging and telehealth. The nearest full VA medical center is the Ralph H. Johnson VA Medical Center at 109 Bee Street in Charleston."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does where I buy change how far I am from a hospital?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and it is worth checking before you choose an area. The hospitals sit at Myrtle Beach, Carolina Forest, Conway, Little River, Murrells Inlet, Loris and Georgetown, with free-standing emergency rooms between them. Ask us for the drive from any specific address you are considering."}}]}</script>
