 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/weather/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How hot are Myrtle Beach summers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The normal summer high is about 86 degrees, with about 21 days a year reaching 90 and almost none reaching 100. July normals at the North Myrtle Beach station are 87.6 for the high and 73.7 for the low. The heat is humid, so it reads hotter than the number."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does it snow in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About an inch a year on average, and most years none. The weather service snowfall database shows 87.4 total inches since 1940. The record is 14 inches in December 1989, and the 5 inch storm of January 2025 was the biggest in 35 years. Another 5 inches fell in early 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is winter like in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"January normals are a 55.7 degree high and a 36.7 low at the North Myrtle Beach station, with about 34 nights a year at or below freezing. The beach stays open, the boardwalk stays open, and the tourist crowds are gone."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How warm is the ocean in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the government pier gauge, roughly 50 degrees in January and February, upper 60s by late April, and upper 70s to mid 80s from June through September. October still averages in the low 70s, and November falls to the mid 60s."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many sunny days does Myrtle Beach get?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The 215 sunny days figure that circulates online is a commercial estimate, not a government one. The nearest long term government station shows about 111 clear days a year and 62 percent of possible sunshine, well above Great Lakes and inland Northeast cities on the same measure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How humid is Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Humid in summer. The nearest station with long term humidity records shows morning humidity around 85 to 88 percent in July and August. July dew points at the closest hourly station average around 73 degrees, which is what makes 87 feel heavy."}}]}</script>
