 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/va-loans/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the benefits of a VA loan in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VA loans offer 0% down payment, no private mortgage insurance, seller concessions up to 4% of the loan amount, and lifetime-reusable entitlement. There is no maximum loan amount with full entitlement. South Carolina also provides property tax relief for qualifying disabled veterans, which can significantly reduce annual carrying costs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a VA loan on a condo in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, but the condo building must be on the VA-approved condo list. Not all buildings qualify. Your lender can check the VA approval status of any specific building. If a building is not approved, VA financing is not available for units in that building regardless of your eligibility. We check VA condo approval status on every building we show to veteran buyers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Palmetto Heroes program and who qualifies?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Palmetto Heroes is an SC Housing program. In 2026 it gave qualifying buyers $10,000 in forgivable down payment assistance with a fixed-rate first mortgage. The 2026 round closed on April 13, 2026, and SC Housing says to watch for a 2027 round in the spring. Eligible professions included teachers, nurses, law enforcement and corrections officers, firefighters, EMTs and paramedics, active-duty military, National Guard members and veterans. Horry County is a targeted county. You can have owned a home in the past three years, but you cannot own another home at closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a good market for military retirees?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Myrtle Beach has a significant and growing military retiree population. Four things make it one of the more financially favorable retirement destinations in the Southeast. There is no state tax on Social Security income, and property taxes on primary residences are low with the 4% owner-occupied rate. Housing is affordable relative to comparable coastal markets, and VA medical facilities at SC bases are close."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use my VA loan more than once?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. VA loan entitlement is reusable. If you have paid off a previous VA loan and sold the property, your full entitlement is restored. If you still have an active VA loan on another property, you may have remaining entitlement available for a second purchase. A VA-approved lender can check your Certificate of Eligibility to confirm your available entitlement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Not checking VA condo approval before making an offer","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"VA financing requires that the condo building be on the VA-approved list. Many buyers make offers on condos, get emotionally invested, and then discover the building is not VA-approved. This forces a last-minute switch to conventional financing, often requiring a higher down payment or killing the deal entirely. Check VA approval before you tour any condo."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Combining VA loan with a DPA program without understanding the rate impact","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Down payment help can change the rate on the first mortgage. SC Housing offers a lower rate on some of its loans taken without its down payment help. Before you add down payment help to a VA loan, ask your lender to quote the loan both ways. Compare the total cost over the years you expect to keep the home."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Underestimating the VA funding fee","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most VA borrowers pay a one-time VA funding fee at closing, a percentage of the loan that varies with first or subsequent use and with any down payment you choose to make; putting more down shrinks it. Disabled veterans with a service-connected disability rating are exempt. This fee can be rolled into the loan but adds to your total loan balance. Factor it into your total cost of purchase."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Not requesting property tax exemptions after closing","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"South Carolina property tax relief for disabled veterans does not apply automatically. You must apply through the Horry County Auditor's office after closing. Qualifying disabled veterans can receive a full property tax exemption on their primary residence. This application is easy to complete but is missed by many buyers who are not aware it exists."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can VA loans be used in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. VA loans work for primary residences across the Grand Strand, including many condos, and the military community around Market Common uses them heavily."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do VA loans require a down payment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No down payment is required for eligible borrowers with full entitlement, and the VA funding fee can be financed into the loan. Veterans with qualifying disability ratings are typically exempt from the funding fee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a VA loan for a condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if the project is VA-approved or becomes approved during the purchase. Many Grand Strand buildings already hold approval, and others can be submitted for review."}}]}</script>
