+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-rules/#article","headline":"Where Airbnb Is Legal in Myrtle Beach, City by City","description":"Short-term rental rules for every Grand Strand jurisdiction in 2026: where STRs are allowed, what licenses they need, the full tax stack per city, and the changes in progress.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-rules/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-07-19","dateModified":"2026-10-27","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-rules/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Grand Strand short-term rental regulations"},"keywords":"Myrtle Beach short-term rental rules, Airbnb laws Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach STR ordinance, Horry County vacation rental rules"}</script>
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-rules/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are Airbnbs legal in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Depends which Myrtle Beach. Inside the city, short-term rentals are prohibited in every residential zoning district except one (RMV), with fewer than 30 grandfathered houses; they operate legally in the commercial and resort districts along the oceanside corridor. Most of what people call Myrtle Beach is unincorporated Horry County, where there is no county STR ordinance at all and the HOA is usually the only restriction. The parcel's jurisdiction is the first thing we check."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a license to run a short-term rental on the Grand Strand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In every jurisdiction except the Town of Pawleys Island, yes: a local business license (city or county), plus a South Carolina retail license from the Department of Revenue to remit accommodations taxes. Surfside Beach doubles its license rates for non-resident owners. Horry County also expects a personal property return on your furnishings each April."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What taxes does a short-term rental collect in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Total lodging tax runs 11 to 13 percent depending on jurisdiction. City of Myrtle Beach is highest at 13 percent, North Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach, Conway, and unincorporated Horry County are 12, and Pawleys Island and unincorporated Georgetown County are 11. The tax applies to stays under 90 days; rentals of 90 or more continuous days to the same person are exempt."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Airbnb collect the taxes for me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only some of them. Airbnb automatically collects the state-administered taxes and several local ones, including Horry County's hospitality fee and the Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, and Surfside city taxes. It does not collect for Pawleys Island or Georgetown County, and platform coverage differs by tax line, so most owners still owe at least one direct filing. We map the exact filings for the specific address before you buy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an HOA ban short-term rentals even where the city allows them?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Covenants and master deeds override what zoning permits, and in unincorporated Horry County, where the county imposes no STR rules, the HOA document is usually the only thing that decides the question. Reading it is part of the building and neighborhood review we run before any offer."}}]}</script>
