-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">1</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Buy below market.</strong> Work with Chapter3 to find <a href="/invest/foreclosures/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">houses in distress</a> and priced under the market. What you pay sets your profit before any work starts.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">2</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Price the repairs before you offer.</strong> Get a contractor&#x27;s number, not an estimate of your own.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">3</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Monitor holding costs while the work runs.</strong> Every extra month is another month of loan payments, taxes and insurance.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">4</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Work with Chapter3 to sell the finished house.</strong> Price it against what closed nearby, not against what is listed.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">5</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Pay the tax.</strong> A flip is inventory, not investment property, so it does not qualify for a 1031 exchange.</p></li></ol><p sty