+<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/strategies/">Strategies</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Small Multifamily</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Strategy</p><h1 class="detail-h1">How to buy a duplex or fourplex<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">in Myrtle Beach.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Chapter3 Realty &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Two, three or four rent checks from one Myrtle Beach building, financed like a regular home: how to buy a duplex, triplex or fourplex here, and who rents the units.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Talk through a building</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
 <p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The five steps</p>
 <h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How small multifamily works, step by step</h2><ol style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.6rem 0;padding:0;max-width:720px"><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">1</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Find a building of two to four units.</strong> Four units or fewer keeps it on a regular home loan.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">2</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Add up the rent roll.</strong> That is the combined rent from every unit, not the best one.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">3</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Weigh it against the whole building&#x27;s costs.</strong> Payment, taxes, insurance and maintenance for all units together.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">4</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Decide whether you will live in one.</strong> Living in a unit opens owner-occupied loans with far less money down.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">5</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Budget for more tenants.</strong> More units means more calls, and one roof or HVAC bill hits every unit at once.</p></li></ol>
 <p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:1rem">Small multifamily means a duplex, triplex, or fourplex. That is two, three, or four homes in one purchase, one loan, one roof. On the Grand Strand, these buildings cluster in Conway, the older parts of Myrtle Beach, and pockets of North Myrtle Beach. Chapter3 has sold in all three Grand Strand pockets and knows which blocks rent to year-round workers and which fill with summer staff. The boxes below give the ten-second version of the trade.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem;margin-top:1rem">How scarce they are: the whole Grand Strand MLS usually shows fewer than one hundred multifamily listings of any size at a time, starting near $225,000 for a small duplex and running past $13 million for hotel-scale property. The two-to-four-unit slice of that is smaller still. That is why the good ones go under contract fast. It is also why Chapter3 watches the Grand Strand MLS for them daily and hears about some before they list, from the agents and property managers our team has worked with here for decades.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Who rents the units: year-round workers, and in summer the J-1 exchange students who staff the beach. J-1 groups rent by the person and fill a unit completely; the demand, the rates and the rules are on our <a href="/invest/j1-rentals/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">J-1 rental guide</a>.
