 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Conway, SC good for real estate investing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For long-term rentals, yes. Conway has the lowest entry prices on the Grand Strand, year-round tenant demand from Coastal Carolina University and local workers, and true fixer-upper inventory for BRRRR investors. It is not a short-term rental market, so estimate monthly rent, not nightly rates."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Conway better for long-term or short-term rentals?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Its inland location and Coastal Carolina University nearby support more long-term and student rental demand than short-term tourism."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why consider Conway?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Pricing is generally more approachable than the oceanfront markets, with a historic downtown along the Waccamaw River."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Conway a good short-term rental market?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Conway is inland and allows rentals under city and county rules, but it is a long-term-rental market driven by Coastal Carolina University and a year-round workforce, not an oceanfront vacation market. Most investors here run annual leases."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Conway flood?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Parts of it can. The Waccamaw River runs through downtown Conway, and the city saw serious river flooding after Hurricanes Matthew (2016) and Florence (2018). Some areas require flood insurance, and Chapter3 will check the FEMA flood map and flood history for the address."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why is Conway cheaper than the beach towns?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It is inland, about 15 miles from the ocean, with a mix of historic homes and new construction, so buyers get more house and land for the money than in oceanfront submarkets."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are property taxes on a second home in Conway?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In the city of Conway that makes a second home's bill about 2.5 times a primary home's on the same house."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which schools serve Conway?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Public schools fall within the Conway attendance area of Horry County Schools, and the city is home to Coastal Carolina University and Horry-Georgetown Technical College. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map."}}]}</script>
