 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is Murrells Inlet known for?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Its waterfront and the MarshWalk dining scene, blending tourism with year-round local living."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What property types are in Murrells Inlet?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A range, from waterfront property to more conventional inland neighborhoods."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are short-term rentals allowed in Murrells Inlet?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. On the Georgetown County side a rental under 30 days is treated as a residential use with no special short-term-rental permit in most zones, though you need a county business license and must remit accommodations tax. The Horry County side follows Horry's unincorporated rules, and an HOA can restrict rentals in either county, and Chapter3 will verify the zoning and pull the HOA documents for the exact address."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which county is Murrells Inlet in?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Both. Murrells Inlet is unincorporated and straddles Horry County to the north and Georgetown County to the south, which changes short-term-rental rules, school assignment, and county taxes depending on the address."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are property taxes like on a second home in Murrells Inlet?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Higher than on a primary residence. A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In Murrells Inlet that makes a second home's bill about 3 times a primary home's on the same house."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which schools serve Murrells Inlet?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on the county side. Horry-side addresses are generally served by the St. James schools in Horry County Schools, and Georgetown-side addresses by the Waccamaw schools in the Georgetown County School District. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment for an address on the district boundary map."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Murrells Inlet a buyer's or seller's market?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "As of mid-2026 it is a buyer's market, with elevated inventory and homes taking well longer than the national norm to sell, which gives buyers room to negotiate."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Murrells Inlet have a beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not a wide public beach of its own. Murrells Inlet is built around a saltwater estuary and the MarshWalk, and the nearest wide public beach access is a short drive north in Garden City."}}]}</script>
