 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is Pawleys Island like?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Historic and low-key, with higher price points and more of a second-home and long-term character than mass tourism."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Who buys in Pawleys Island?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Buyers drawn to a quieter, established feel, often for second homes or longer-term ownership."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you short-term rental in Pawleys Island?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Generally yes. There is no permanent ban. The only ban was a temporary 2020 COVID measure. The incorporated Town of Pawleys Island governs the barrier island and Georgetown County governs the mainland, and gated communities can add their own limits, and Chapter3 will verify the jurisdiction and pull the HOA rules by address."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Pawleys Island in Georgetown County?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Pawleys Island is in Georgetown County, about 25 miles south of Myrtle Beach, split between the small incorporated town on the island and unincorporated mainland communities."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Pawleys Island expensive?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It is the upscale end of the southern Strand. The home-value index sat near $514,000 in mid-2026, with waterfront and gated-community homes running much higher and DeBordieu reaching into the multi-millions."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How bad is flood risk in Pawleys Island?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "High. Public data flags around 89 percent of properties as facing severe flood risk over 30 years, so flood insurance and elevation certificates are essential considerations for any purchase."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which schools serve Pawleys Island?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Public schools fall within the Georgetown County School District, generally the Waccamaw schools for the Litchfield and Pawleys area. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map."}}]}</script>
